      "title": "France hopes to send ‘strategic signal’ about Europe’s renewed military focus at Bastille Day celebrations – Europe live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/jul/14/france-bastille-day-emmanuel-macron-volodymyr-zelenskyy-germany-brussels-eu-albania-moldova-montenegro-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Many leaders from the ‘Coalition of the Willing’ stayed overnight in Paris to attend the parade, which will be Emmanuel Macron’s last as president</p><p><strong>Here is the first big moment of the day as the Garde républicaine plays the French national anthem, “La Marseillaise”.</strong></p><p><strong>Macron</strong> is not singing, but <strong>Lecornu </strong>behind him – very much is.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/jul/14/france-bastille-day-emmanuel-macron-volodymyr-zelenskyy-germany-brussels-eu-albania-moldova-montenegro-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
